            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic value of negative dobutamine stress echo in women with intermediate probability of coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-2, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Women with an intermediate pretest probability of coronary artery disease represent a significant proportion of patients referred for the investigation of chest pain. Dobutamine stress echocardiography can be used to restratify these patients into a low-risk group without resorting to cardiac catheterization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
